# module.exports = fromMain; require("./early.cjs"); one()   with   one() { two() }  two() { three() }  three() { require(name)() }   built with two entry points, main.cjs and second.cjs
# A module is required under a name nobody knows only in a function that is entered late, after modules have run. The load evaluates nothing: the file that nothing else names stays unreached.
